IMPORT prelude

-- Workplace Injury Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 2013 (Vic) -- seat-neutral core.
--
-- Edition: Act No. 67/2013, Version No. 054, as at 2 October 2026 (includes the WorkCover Scheme Modernisation
-- amendments, No. 8/2024, ss 4-26 in force 31 March 2024), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/workplace-injury-rehabilitation-and-compensation-act-2013.txt, a plain-text
-- conversion of the Word file the owner saved by hand on 2026-11-06. Line numbers below are lines of that file.
--
-- FIGURES. The Act prints its dollar amounts as they stood when each was written, and Division 1 of Part 13
-- (ss 542-547, lines 7709-7834) varies them every 1 July. The varied amounts for 1 July 2025 to 30 June 2026 and
-- 1 July 2026 to 30 June 2027 are taken from the Victoria Government Gazette No. S 363 of 30 June 2026, deposited in
-- subjects/au/vic/workers-compensation-annual-indexation-notice/ (GG2026S363.txt, the 2013 Act notice at lines
-- 389-733). They are copied here by hand, with the Gazette line, because IMPORT cannot reach another subject's
-- folder. A day outside those two years answers NOTHING.
--
-- BASELINE. Written straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill, design defaults of
-- 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as
-- advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Workplace Injury Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 2013 (Vic) -- seat-neutral core`

§§ `Dates`

-- A period "after" a day does not count that day (the reading of the Interpretation of Legislation Act 1984 (Vic)
-- s 44, which is not deposited). So "within 30 days after" a day ends 30 days later; "within the period of 2 years
-- after" a day ends on the same date 2 years later; "cannot be made before the expiry of the period of 12 months
-- after" a day can first be done the day after the same date 12 months later. READING, recorded in NOTES.md.
GIVEN `n` IS A NUMBER, `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`days after` `n` `the day` MEANS DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL `the day` PLUS `n`)

GIVEN `the earlier day` IS A DATE, `the later day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`days from` `the earlier day` `to` `the later day` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `the later day` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `the earlier day`

GIVEN `a` IS A DATE, `b` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a` `is on or before` `b` IF DATE_SERIAL `a` AT MOST DATE_SERIAL `b`

GIVEN `the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a leap year` `the year` IF
        ((`the year` MODULO 4) EQUALS 0 AND (NOT ((`the year` MODULO 100) EQUALS 0)))
    OR  (`the year` MODULO 400) EQUALS 0

GIVEN `the month` IS A NUMBER, `the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the last day of month` `the month` `the year` MEANS
    IF `the month` EQUALS 2
    THEN IF `is a leap year` `the year` THEN 29 ELSE 28
    ELSE IF `the month` EQUALS 4 OR `the month` EQUALS 6 OR `the month` EQUALS 9 OR `the month` EQUALS 11
         THEN 30
         ELSE 31

-- The same date n months later; where that month is shorter, its last day (31 August + 6 months: 28 or 29 February).
GIVEN `n` IS A NUMBER, `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`months after` `n` `the day` MEANS
    DATE_FROM_DMY
        (min (DATE_DAY `the day`) (`the last day of month` `the new month` `the new year`))
        `the new month`
        `the new year`
    WHERE
        `the month index` MEANS (DATE_YEAR `the day` TIMES 12) PLUS (DATE_MONTH `the day` MINUS 1) PLUS `n`
        `the new month` MEANS (`the month index` MODULO 12) PLUS 1
        `the new year` MEANS (`the month index` MINUS (`the month index` MODULO 12)) DIVIDED BY 12

GIVEN `n` IS A NUMBER, `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`years after` `n` `the day` MEANS `months after` (`n` TIMES 12) `the day`

-- s 329A (line 5165): "In calculating a period of time for the purpose of section 330, 331, 332, 333, 334, 335 or
-- 337, the period from 24 December to 9 January next following must be disregarded."
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `falls in the period from 24 December to 9 January` `the day` IF
        (DATE_MONTH `the day` EQUALS 12 AND DATE_DAY `the day` AT LEAST 24)
    OR  (DATE_MONTH `the day` EQUALS 1 AND DATE_DAY `the day` AT MOST 9)

-- The day n counted days after a day, not counting any day from 24 December to 9 January (s 329A).
GIVEN `n` IS A NUMBER, `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`days after, disregarding 24 December to 9 January,` `n` `the day` MEANS
    IF `n` AT MOST 0
    THEN `the day`
    ELSE IF `falls in the period from 24 December to 9 January` (`days after` 1 `the day`)
         THEN `days after, disregarding 24 December to 9 January,` `n` (`days after` 1 `the day`)
         ELSE `days after, disregarding 24 December to 9 January,` (`n` MINUS 1) (`days after` 1 `the day`)

§§ `Division 1 of Part 13 -- the varied amounts, from the Gazette notice of 30 June 2026`

-- The two years the deposited Gazette notice prints: "Rate before 1 July 2026" (read as 1 July 2025 to
-- 30 June 2026) and "Rate from 1 July 2026" (read as 1 July 2026 to 30 June 2027), the reading of the notice's own
-- encoding (workers-compensation-annual-indexation-notice/encodings/baseline-2026-10, "The period rule").
DECLARE `Figures year` IS ONE OF
    `the year from 1 July 2025`
    `the year from 1 July 2026`

GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE `Figures year`
`the figures year for` `the day` MEANS
    IF      (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 7 2025) `is on or before` `the day`
        AND `the day` `is on or before` (DATE_FROM_DMY 30 6 2026)
    THEN JUST `the year from 1 July 2025`
    ELSE IF     (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 7 2026) `is on or before` `the day`
            AND `the day` `is on or before` (DATE_FROM_DMY 30 6 2027)
         THEN JUST `the year from 1 July 2026`
         ELSE NOTHING

-- Each amount, the Act's own figure (from the s 544 or s 545 Table, lines 7737-7754 and 7756-7823) and the Gazette
-- line of the varied figures.
DECLARE `Varied amount` IS ONE OF
    `twice the State average weekly earnings`                 -- s 159; Gazette s 161(a)(ii), line 498
    `the minimum current weekly earnings in ss 164 and 165`   -- Act $177 (s 544 items 1-2); Gazette lines 518, 522
    `the s 211(2)(b) starting amount`                         -- Act $11 670; Gazette line 534
    `the s 211(2)(b) amount for each percentage point`        -- Act $9940; Gazette line 536
    `the s 211(2)(c) and s 212(b) starting amount`            -- Act $18 810; Gazette lines 540, 559
    `the s 211(2)(c) and s 212(b) amount for each percentage point` -- Act $2830; Gazette lines 541, 560
    `the s 211(2)(d) and s 212(c) starting amount`            -- Act $75 260; Gazette lines 548, 561
    `the s 211(2)(d) and s 212(c) amount for each percentage point` -- Act $4700; Gazette lines 549, 562
    `the s 211(2)(e) and s 212(d) starting amount`            -- Act $262 070; Gazette lines 550, 565
    `the s 211(2)(e) and s 212(d) amount for each percentage point` -- Act $29 330; Gazette lines 551, 566
    `the maximum for non-economic loss`                       -- Act $555 350 (ss 211(2)(e)(ii), (f), 217) and $555 530 (s 212(d)(ii), (e)); Gazette lines 552, 555, 567, 570, 603, 605
    `the lump sum on the death of a worker`                   -- Act $555 350 (s 236(1)-(6)); Gazette lines 417-442
    `the s 236(3)(a) amount for the one dependent child`      -- Act $55 530; Gazette line 425
    `the s 236(4)(a) amount for each dependent child`         -- Act $27 770; Gazette line 432
    `the s 236(5)(a) amount for the dependent partners`       -- Act $416 520; Gazette line 440
    `the s 237A(1) amount for each close family member`       -- Act $10 000; Gazette line 451
    `the s 340(a)(i) pecuniary loss threshold`                -- Act $56 650; Gazette line 699
    `the s 340(a)(ii) pecuniary loss maximum`                 -- Act $1 275 570; Gazette line 700
    `the s 340(b)(i) pain and suffering threshold`            -- Act $54 730; Gazette line 702
    `the s 340(b)(ii) pain and suffering maximum`             -- Act $555 350; Gazette line 703

GIVEN `the amount` IS A `Varied amount`, `the year` IS A `Figures year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the varied amount` `the amount` `for` `the year` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the year`
    WHEN `the year from 1 July 2025` THEN
        CONSIDER `the amount`
        WHEN `twice the State average weekly earnings` THEN 2930
        WHEN `the minimum current weekly earnings in ss 164 and 165` THEN 251
        WHEN `the s 211(2)(b) starting amount` THEN 15940
        WHEN `the s 211(2)(b) amount for each percentage point` THEN 13580
        WHEN `the s 211(2)(c) and s 212(b) starting amount` THEN 25730
        WHEN `the s 211(2)(c) and s 212(b) amount for each percentage point` THEN 3860
        WHEN `the s 211(2)(d) and s 212(c) starting amount` THEN 102950
        WHEN `the s 211(2)(d) and s 212(c) amount for each percentage point` THEN 6440
        WHEN `the s 211(2)(e) and s 212(d) starting amount` THEN 358420
        WHEN `the s 211(2)(e) and s 212(d) amount for each percentage point` THEN 40120
        WHEN `the maximum for non-economic loss` THEN 759510
        WHEN `the lump sum on the death of a worker` THEN 759510
        WHEN `the s 236(3)(a) amount for the one dependent child` THEN 75940
        WHEN `the s 236(4)(a) amount for each dependent child` THEN 37990
        WHEN `the s 236(5)(a) amount for the dependent partners` THEN 569650
        WHEN `the s 237A(1) amount for each close family member` THEN 10000
        WHEN `the s 340(a)(i) pecuniary loss threshold` THEN 77490
        WHEN `the s 340(a)(ii) pecuniary loss maximum` THEN 1744530
        WHEN `the s 340(b)(i) pain and suffering threshold` THEN 74820
        WHEN `the s 340(b)(ii) pain and suffering maximum` THEN 759510
    WHEN `the year from 1 July 2026` THEN
        CONSIDER `the amount`
        WHEN `twice the State average weekly earnings` THEN 3000
        WHEN `the minimum current weekly earnings in ss 164 and 165` THEN 257
        WHEN `the s 211(2)(b) starting amount` THEN 16430
        WHEN `the s 211(2)(b) amount for each percentage point` THEN 14000
        WHEN `the s 211(2)(c) and s 212(b) starting amount` THEN 26530
        WHEN `the s 211(2)(c) and s 212(b) amount for each percentage point` THEN 3980
        WHEN `the s 211(2)(d) and s 212(c) starting amount` THEN 106130
        WHEN `the s 211(2)(d) and s 212(c) amount for each percentage point` THEN 6640
        WHEN `the s 211(2)(e) and s 212(d) starting amount` THEN 369510
        WHEN `the s 211(2)(e) and s 212(d) amount for each percentage point` THEN 41360
        WHEN `the maximum for non-economic loss` THEN 783000
        WHEN `the lump sum on the death of a worker` THEN 783000
        WHEN `the s 236(3)(a) amount for the one dependent child` THEN 78290
        WHEN `the s 236(4)(a) amount for each dependent child` THEN 39170
        WHEN `the s 236(5)(a) amount for the dependent partners` THEN 587270
        WHEN `the s 237A(1) amount for each close family member` THEN 10310
        WHEN `the s 340(a)(i) pecuniary loss threshold` THEN 79890
        WHEN `the s 340(a)(ii) pecuniary loss maximum` THEN 1798500
        WHEN `the s 340(b)(i) pain and suffering threshold` THEN 77130
        WHEN `the s 340(b)(ii) pain and suffering maximum` THEN 783000

-- The amount in force on a day, or NOTHING outside the two years the deposited notice prints.
GIVEN `the amount` IS A `Varied amount`, `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the varied amount` `the amount` `on` `the day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the figures year for` `the day`
    WHEN JUST `y` THEN JUST (`the varied amount` `the amount` `for` `y`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

§§ `Part 2 Division 3 -- entitlement to compensation (ss 37, 39, 40, 625(1))`

DECLARE `Kind of injury` IS ONE OF
    `a physical injury`
    `a mental injury`   -- s 3 (line 217): an injury that causes significant behavioural, cognitive or psychological dysfunction, diagnosed by a medical practitioner under the latest DSM

-- s 40(7) (lines 827-837): "severe injury means any of the following" -- a closed list.
DECLARE `Severe injury head` IS ONE OF
    `a significant acquired permanent brain injury`
    `permanent paraplegia`
    `permanent quadriplegia`
    `amputation of a limb, hand or foot`
    `full thickness burns causing permanent severe disfigurement or a significant permanent inability for daily living`
    `an injury that results in permanent blindness`
    `a brachial plexus injury resulting in permanent effective loss of the use of a limb`
    `a physical internal injury resulting in a significant permanent inability for daily living`
    `none of these`

GIVEN `the head` IS A `Severe injury head`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 40(7) -- is a severe injury` `the head` IF
    CONSIDER `the head`
    WHEN `none of these` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 625(1) (line 9263) and the endnote for No. 8/2024 (line 10204: "Ss 4-26 on 31.3.24"): the new definition of
-- mental injury and ss 39 and 40 as amended "apply to claims made in respect of injuries that occur on or after"
-- 31 March 2024. For a mental injury before then the earlier text applies, which is not deposited: NOTHING.
`the day the 2024 mental injury amendments commenced` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 31 3 2024

-- s 37(1); s 39(1), (1A), (2A); s 40(1), (1A), (2), (2A), (3), (4), (5), (6). The facts are the ones the sections
-- name; "reasonable" management action and what "may be considered usual or typical" are judgments, answered
-- conditionally as facts the worker states. s 41 (undisclosed pre-existing injury), ss 42-44 (driving offences),
-- ss 47-49 (injury outside Australia, compensation elsewhere) are out (NOTES.md).
GIVEN `employment is connected with Victoria` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the kind of injury` IS A `Kind of injury`
      `the day of the injury` IS A DATE
      `the injury arose out of or in the course of employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the mental injury predominantly arose out of or in the course of employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the mental injury was caused wholly or predominantly by reasonable management action` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the mental injury was predominantly caused by work related stress or burnout from usual or typical events` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the mental injury was predominantly caused by usual or typical traumatic events in the worker's duties` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the injury is a recurrence or aggravation of a pre-existing mental injury` IS A BOOLEAN
      `employment was the predominant cause of the recurrence or aggravation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the injury is a heart attack, stroke, disease, or recurrence or aggravation of a pre-existing physical injury or disease` IS A BOOLEAN
      `employment was a significant contributing factor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is proved the injury was deliberately or wilfully self-inflicted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is proved the injury is attributable to the worker's serious and wilful misconduct` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the injury results in death or severe injury` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ss 37, 39, 40 -- the worker is entitled to compensation` MEANS
    IF NOT `employment is connected with Victoria`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- s 37(1): "There is no entitlement to compensation under this Act other than in respect of employment that is connected with this State."
    ELSE CONSIDER `the kind of injury`
         WHEN `a mental injury` THEN
            IF DATE_SERIAL `the day of the injury` LESS THAN DATE_SERIAL `the day the 2024 mental injury amendments commenced`
            THEN NOTHING
            ELSE JUST (    (   `the mental injury predominantly arose out of or in the course of employment`
                            OR `the mental injury was predominantly caused by usual or typical traumatic events in the worker's duties`)
                       AND (NOT `the mental injury was caused wholly or predominantly by reasonable management action`)
                       AND (NOT (    `the mental injury was predominantly caused by work related stress or burnout from usual or typical events`
                                 AND (NOT `the mental injury was predominantly caused by usual or typical traumatic events in the worker's duties`)))
                       AND (NOT (    `the injury is a recurrence or aggravation of a pre-existing mental injury`
                                 AND (NOT `employment was the predominant cause of the recurrence or aggravation`)))
                       AND `s 40(4), (5), (6) -- not barred by self-infliction or misconduct` `it is proved the injury was deliberately or wilfully self-inflicted` `it is proved the injury is attributable to the worker's serious and wilful misconduct` `the injury results in death or severe injury`)
         WHEN `a physical injury` THEN
            JUST (    `the injury arose out of or in the course of employment`
                  AND (NOT (    `the injury is a heart attack, stroke, disease, or recurrence or aggravation of a pre-existing physical injury or disease`
                            AND (NOT `employment was a significant contributing factor`)))
                  AND `s 40(4), (5), (6) -- not barred by self-infliction or misconduct` `it is proved the injury was deliberately or wilfully self-inflicted` `it is proved the injury is attributable to the worker's serious and wilful misconduct` `the injury results in death or severe injury`)

-- s 40(4): deliberately or wilfully self-inflicted, proved: no entitlement. s 40(5): serious and wilful misconduct,
-- proved: no entitlement; s 40(6): "Subsection (5) does not apply if the injury results in death or severe injury."
GIVEN `self-inflicted` IS A BOOLEAN, `misconduct` IS A BOOLEAN, `death or severe injury` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 40(4), (5), (6) -- not barred by self-infliction or misconduct` `self-inflicted` `misconduct` `death or severe injury` IF
        (NOT `self-inflicted`)
    AND (NOT (`misconduct` AND (NOT `death or severe injury`)))

§§ `Part 2 Division 1 -- notice of injury and the claim (ss 18, 20)`

-- s 18(7): reasons that are "to be taken not to have been reasonably practicable" -- a list the text closes for its
-- own purpose ("Without limiting the generality of subsection (6)(a)").
DECLARE `Reason for late notice` IS ONE OF
    `ignorance or a mistake`
    `undue influence or duress`
    `being absent from Victoria`
    `none of these`

DECLARE `Notice outcome` IS ONE OF
    `notice was given in time (s 18(1))`
    `notice was late, and the Authority or self-insurer waived or extended the time (s 18(6))`
    `notice was late; s 18(7) treats it as not reasonably practicable, a ground on which the Authority or self-insurer may waive or extend the time (s 18(6)(a))`
    `notice was late: no compensation unless the Authority or self-insurer is satisfied of a ground in s 18(6) and waives or extends the time (s 18(5))`

-- s 18(1) (line 542): notice "must be given by the person to the employer within 30 days after the person becomes
-- aware of the injury". s 18(3): entering the workplace particulars in the register of injuries is notice.
GIVEN `the day the worker became aware of the injury` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 18(1) -- the last day for notice of injury` `the day the worker became aware of the injury` MEANS
    `days after` 30 `the day the worker became aware of the injury`

-- s 18(5), (6), (7).
GIVEN `the day the worker became aware of the injury` IS A DATE
      `the day notice was given or the particulars were entered in the register` IS A DATE
      `the Authority or self-insurer has waived or extended the time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reason notice was late` IS A `Reason for late notice`
GIVETH A `Notice outcome`
`s 18(5)-(7) -- the effect of the time notice was given` `the day the worker became aware of the injury` `the day notice was given or the particulars were entered in the register` `the Authority or self-insurer has waived or extended the time` `the reason notice was late` MEANS
    IF `the day notice was given or the particulars were entered in the register` `is on or before` (`s 18(1) -- the last day for notice of injury` `the day the worker became aware of the injury`)
    THEN `notice was given in time (s 18(1))`
    ELSE IF `the Authority or self-insurer has waived or extended the time`
         THEN `notice was late, and the Authority or self-insurer waived or extended the time (s 18(6))`
         ELSE CONSIDER `the reason notice was late`
              WHEN `none of these` THEN `notice was late: no compensation unless the Authority or self-insurer is satisfied of a ground in s 18(6) and waives or extends the time (s 18(5))`
              OTHERWISE `notice was late; s 18(7) treats it as not reasonably practicable, a ground on which the Authority or self-insurer may waive or extend the time (s 18(6)(a))`

DECLARE `Kind of claim` IS ONE OF
    `a claim for weekly payments`
    `a claim for compensation for the death of a worker`   -- ss 235, 236, 237, 237AA, 237A, 241
    `a claim for medical and like services`                -- Division 7 of Part 5
    `a claim for an impairment benefit`                     -- Division 5 of Part 5 (no time limit in s 20(8))

-- s 20(8) (lines 578-582). (a) weekly payments: "as soon as practicable after the incapacity arising from the injury
-- becomes known" -- no day fixed: NOTHING. (b) death: "within the period of 2 years after the date of the death".
-- (c) medical and like services: "within 6 months after the date of the relevant service". s 20(8) sets no limit
-- for a Division 5 claim: NOTHING. s 20(9): the Authority or self-insurer may waive or extend for a "special excuse".
GIVEN `the kind of claim` IS A `Kind of claim`
      `the day of the worker's death` IS A DATE
      `the day of the service` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 20(8) -- the last day to make the claim` `the kind of claim` `the day of the worker's death` `the day of the service` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the kind of claim`
    WHEN `a claim for compensation for the death of a worker` THEN JUST (`years after` 2 `the day of the worker's death`)
    WHEN `a claim for medical and like services` THEN JUST (`months after` 6 `the day of the service`)
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

§§ `Part 3 Division 3 -- the decision on a claim (ss 75, 75A, 178)`

DECLARE `WIRC party` IS ONE OF
    `the worker`
    `the employer`
    `the Authority or self-insurer`
    `a court`

DECLARE `WIRC action` IS ONE OF
    `give the employer notice of the injury`
    `acknowledge the notice in writing`
    `give written notice of its decision on the claim` HAS `the claim is accepted` IS A BOOLEAN
    `begin paying weekly payments`
    `decide the application under s 165`
    `advise the worker in writing on the serious injury application`
    `apply to a court for leave to bring proceedings for damages`
    `ask the Authority to consent to a late application for leave`

-- s 75(1) (line 1405): "within 28 days after receiving the claim" (with a medical certificate) or "within 28 days
-- after receiving such a medical certificate".
GIVEN `the day the claim was received` IS A DATE
      `the claim came with a medical certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the medical certificate was received` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 75(1) -- the last day for a decision on a weekly payments claim` `the day the claim was received` `the claim came with a medical certificate` `the day the medical certificate was received` MEANS
    IF `the claim came with a medical certificate`
    THEN `days after` 28 `the day the claim was received`
    ELSE `days after` 28 `the day the medical certificate was received`

-- s 75(1): if no written notice of a decision is given in time, "the claim is deemed to have been accepted".
GIVEN `the last day for a decision` IS A DATE
      `written notice of a decision has been given` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day written notice of the decision was given` IS A DATE
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 75(1) -- the claim is deemed accepted` `the last day for a decision` `written notice of a decision has been given` `the day written notice of the decision was given` `the day asked about` IF
        (NOT (`the day asked about` `is on or before` `the last day for a decision`))
    AND (   (NOT `written notice of a decision has been given`)
         OR (NOT (`the day written notice of the decision was given` `is on or before` `the last day for a decision`)))

-- s 178(3) (line 2736): accepted claim, payments "must commence to be paid within 7 days after the claim is accepted".
GIVEN `the day the claim was accepted` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 178(3) -- the last day for weekly payments to begin` `the day the claim was accepted` MEANS `days after` 7 `the day the claim was accepted`

-- s 75(1) with s 178(3), as a rule. Clock: days from receiving the claim and certificate. A decision to accept starts
-- the 7 days to pay; a decision to reject ends the matter here (the worker's rights of review are out); silence for
-- 28 days deems the claim accepted, and payments must then begin within 7 days.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `WIRC party` `WIRC action`
`s 75(1), s 178(3) -- the Authority or self-insurer must decide a weekly payments claim within 28 days` MEANS
    PARTY `the Authority or self-insurer`
    MUST  `give written notice of its decision on the claim` `accepted`
    WITHIN 28
    HENCE
        IF `accepted`
        THEN PARTY `the Authority or self-insurer`
             MUST  `begin paying weekly payments`
             WITHIN 7
             LEST  BREACH BY `the Authority or self-insurer` BECAUSE "s 178(3): payments must commence to be paid within 7 days after the claim is accepted"
        ELSE FULFILLED
    LEST
        PARTY `the Authority or self-insurer`
        MUST  `begin paying weekly payments`
        WITHIN 7
        LEST  BREACH BY `the Authority or self-insurer` BECAUSE "s 75(1), s 178(3): no decision within 28 days, so the claim is deemed accepted and payments must commence within 7 days"

-- s 18(1), (4), (5), as a rule. Clock: days from the worker becoming aware of the injury.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `WIRC party` `WIRC action`
`s 18 -- the worker must give notice of the injury within 30 days, and the employer must acknowledge it` MEANS
    PARTY `the worker`
    MUST  `give the employer notice of the injury`
    WITHIN 30
    HENCE
        (PARTY `the employer`
         MUST  `acknowledge the notice in writing`)
    LEST  BREACH BY `the worker` BECAUSE "s 18(1), (5): notice was not given within 30 days after the worker became aware of the injury, so compensation cannot be recovered unless the Authority or self-insurer waives or extends the time (s 18(6))"

§§ `Part 5 Division 10 -- provisional payments for a mental injury (ss 263B, 263I)`

-- Division 10 was inserted by No. 5/2021 s 11, in force 1 July 2021 (endnote, line 10156).
`the day Division 10 of Part 5 commenced` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 7 2021

-- s 263B(1), (2) (lines 3971-3975): a claim for compensation in respect of a mental injury -> the Authority or
-- self-insurer "must pay the reasonable costs of a service specified in section 224(1)(a)" as provisional payments;
-- not if the claim was made before the Division commenced, or the same mental injury and circumstances were
-- determined before (subject to s 263I(1)(b)). s 263AA: the s 3 definition of mental injury does not apply, and the
-- payments are made whether or not the claim is later accepted.
GIVEN `the day of the claim` IS A DATE
      `a claim for the same mental injury and circumstances was determined before` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 263B -- the worker is entitled to provisional payments` `the day of the claim` `a claim for the same mental injury and circumstances was determined before` IF
        `the day Division 10 of Part 5 commenced` `is on or before` `the day of the claim`
    AND (NOT `a claim for the same mental injury and circumstances was determined before`)

-- s 263I(1), (2): payable from the day of the s 75A determination until the day the claim is accepted, or in any
-- other case 13 weeks (91 days) after the determination day.
GIVEN `the day of the determination under s 75A` IS A DATE
      `the claim has been accepted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the claim was accepted` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 263I -- the day provisional payments end` `the day of the determination under s 75A` `the claim has been accepted` `the day the claim was accepted` MEANS
    IF `the claim has been accepted`
    THEN `the day the claim was accepted`
    ELSE `days after` 91 `the day of the determination under s 75A`

§§ `Part 5 Division 2 -- weekly payments (ss 152, 161-166, 169, 171)`

DECLARE `Entitlement period` IS ONE OF
    `the first entitlement period`    -- s 152: an aggregate period not exceeding 13 weeks of weekly payments
    `the second entitlement period`   -- s 152: an aggregate 117 weeks after the first
    `after the second entitlement period`

-- s 152 (lines 2173, 2180, 2181-2186): weeks are weeks "in respect of which any amount of compensation in the form of
-- weekly payments ... is paid or payable, whether for all or any part of that week". The n-th such week.
GIVEN `the week number` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Entitlement period`
`s 152 -- the entitlement period of week` `the week number` MEANS
    IF `the week number` AT MOST 13
    THEN `the first entitlement period`
    ELSE IF `the week number` AT MOST 130
         THEN `the second entitlement period`
         ELSE `after the second entitlement period`

-- s 161 (lines 2323-2332): "(a) if the worker has no current work capacity and no current weekly earnings, at the
-- rate of (i) 95 per cent of the worker's pre-injury average weekly earnings, less the deductible amount; or (ii)
-- twice the State average weekly earnings -- whichever is the lesser; or (b) [otherwise] ... (i) the difference
-- between 95 per cent of the worker's pre-injury average weekly earnings, less the deductible amount and the
-- worker's current weekly earnings; or (ii) the difference between twice the State average weekly earnings and the
-- worker's current weekly earnings -- whichever is the lesser." READING: a difference below nil is nil.
GIVEN `twice SAWE` IS A NUMBER
      `pre-injury average weekly earnings` IS A NUMBER
      `the deductible amount` IS A NUMBER
      `the worker has a current work capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `current weekly earnings` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 161 -- the weekly payment in the first entitlement period` `twice SAWE` `pre-injury average weekly earnings` `the deductible amount` `the worker has a current work capacity` `current weekly earnings` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the worker has a current work capacity`) AND `current weekly earnings` EQUALS 0
    THEN max 0 (min ((0.95 TIMES `pre-injury average weekly earnings`) MINUS `the deductible amount`) `twice SAWE`)
    ELSE max 0 (min (((0.95 TIMES `pre-injury average weekly earnings`) MINUS `the deductible amount`) MINUS `current weekly earnings`) (`twice SAWE` MINUS `current weekly earnings`))

-- s 162 (lines 2334-2343): the same with 80 per cent, and in (b) "80 per cent of the worker's current weekly
-- earnings". s 163(2) and s 165(5) use the s 162(b) rate (with current weekly earnings nil where there are none).
GIVEN `twice SAWE` IS A NUMBER
      `pre-injury average weekly earnings` IS A NUMBER
      `the deductible amount` IS A NUMBER
      `the worker has a current work capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `current weekly earnings` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 162 -- the weekly payment in the second entitlement period` `twice SAWE` `pre-injury average weekly earnings` `the deductible amount` `the worker has a current work capacity` `current weekly earnings` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the worker has a current work capacity`) AND `current weekly earnings` EQUALS 0
    THEN max 0 (min ((0.8 TIMES `pre-injury average weekly earnings`) MINUS `the deductible amount`) `twice SAWE`)
    ELSE max 0 (min (((0.8 TIMES `pre-injury average weekly earnings`) MINUS `the deductible amount`) MINUS (0.8 TIMES `current weekly earnings`)) (`twice SAWE` MINUS (0.8 TIMES `current weekly earnings`)))

-- s 163(1) (lines 2347-2349), as substituted by No. 8/2024 s 13(1): weekly payments cease on the expiry of the second
-- entitlement period "unless the Authority or self-insurer determines that the worker (a) has no current work
-- capacity and is likely to continue indefinitely to have no current work capacity; and (b) has a whole person
-- impairment of more than 20 per cent resulting from one or more compensable injuries". The determination is the
-- Authority's; the facts it turns on are inputs. s 625(2): a worker already receiving weekly payments after the
-- second entitlement period immediately before 31 March 2024 keeps the earlier ss 163, 165 and 175 (not deposited).
GIVEN `no current work capacity, likely to continue indefinitely` IS A BOOLEAN
      `whole person impairment from compensable injuries, per cent` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 163(1) -- the conditions for weekly payments after the second entitlement period are met` `no current work capacity, likely to continue indefinitely` `whole person impairment from compensable injuries, per cent` IF
        `no current work capacity, likely to continue indefinitely`
    AND `whole person impairment from compensable injuries, per cent` GREATER THAN 20

-- s 165(4) (lines 2411-2416): the Authority or self-insurer "must not approve an application ... unless it is
-- satisfied that (a) the worker has returned to work ... for a period of not less than 15 hours per week and is in
-- receipt of current weekly earnings, or current weekly earnings together with non-pecuniary benefits ..., of at
-- least $177 per week [varied: s 544 item 2]; and (b) because of the injury, the worker is, and is likely to continue
-- indefinitely to be, incapable of undertaking further additional employment or work which would increase the
-- worker's current weekly earnings; and (c) the worker has a whole person impairment of more than 20 per cent".
GIVEN `the minimum weekly earnings` IS A NUMBER
      `hours worked each week` IS A NUMBER
      `current weekly earnings with non-pecuniary benefits` IS A NUMBER
      `incapable indefinitely of further work that would increase earnings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `whole person impairment from compensable injuries, per cent` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 165(4) -- the conditions for continuing weekly payments while working are met` `the minimum weekly earnings` `hours worked each week` `current weekly earnings with non-pecuniary benefits` `incapable indefinitely of further work that would increase earnings` `whole person impairment from compensable injuries, per cent` IF
        `hours worked each week` AT LEAST 15
    AND `current weekly earnings with non-pecuniary benefits` AT LEAST `the minimum weekly earnings`
    AND `incapable indefinitely of further work that would increase earnings`
    AND `whole person impairment from compensable injuries, per cent` GREATER THAN 20

-- s 165(3) (line 2407): "within 28 days after receiving the application -- (a) approve or reject the application; and
-- (b) advise the worker in writing". The Act states no consequence for silence (contrast s 75(1)).
GIVETH A DEONTIC `WIRC party` `WIRC action`
`s 165(3) -- the Authority or self-insurer must decide a s 165 application within 28 days` MEANS
    PARTY `the Authority or self-insurer`
    MUST  `decide the application under s 165`
    WITHIN 28
    LEST  BREACH BY `the Authority or self-insurer` BECAUSE "s 165(3): an application under s 165(1) must be approved or rejected, and the worker advised in writing, within 28 days after it is received"

-- The weekly payment for the n-th week of weekly payments. After the second entitlement period: the s 163(2) rate if
-- the s 163(1) determination is made; otherwise the s 165(5) rate if a s 165 application was approved; otherwise
-- nil, because "a worker's entitlement ... ceases upon the expiry of the second entitlement period" (s 163(1)).
-- s 190(3) and s 191(4) (deemed entitlement until a notice expires) and s 164 (surgery) are out (NOTES.md).
GIVEN `twice SAWE` IS A NUMBER
      `the week number` IS A NUMBER
      `pre-injury average weekly earnings` IS A NUMBER
      `the deductible amount` IS A NUMBER
      `the worker has a current work capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `current weekly earnings` IS A NUMBER
      `the s 163(1) determination is made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a s 165 application is approved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`ss 161-165 -- the weekly payment` `twice SAWE` `the week number` `pre-injury average weekly earnings` `the deductible amount` `the worker has a current work capacity` `current weekly earnings` `the s 163(1) determination is made` `a s 165 application is approved` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 152 -- the entitlement period of week` `the week number`
    WHEN `the first entitlement period` THEN `s 161 -- the weekly payment in the first entitlement period` `twice SAWE` `pre-injury average weekly earnings` `the deductible amount` `the worker has a current work capacity` `current weekly earnings`
    WHEN `the second entitlement period` THEN `s 162 -- the weekly payment in the second entitlement period` `twice SAWE` `pre-injury average weekly earnings` `the deductible amount` `the worker has a current work capacity` `current weekly earnings`
    WHEN `after the second entitlement period` THEN
        IF `the s 163(1) determination is made` OR `a s 165 application is approved`
        THEN `s 162 -- the weekly payment in the second entitlement period` `twice SAWE` `pre-injury average weekly earnings` `the deductible amount` TRUE `current weekly earnings`
        ELSE 0

DECLARE `Age limit` IS ONE OF
    `weekly payments stop when the worker reaches retirement age (s 171)`
    `weekly payments for not more than the first 130 weeks of incapacity (s 169)`

-- s 169 (line 2612): injured "within the period of 130 weeks before attaining retirement age or after attaining
-- retirement age" -> "not more than the first 130 weeks (whether consecutive or not) of incapacity". s 171: otherwise
-- no weekly payments after retirement age (subject to s 170, out). s 3: retirement age is pension age under the
-- Social Security Act 1991 (Cth), an input. READING: an injury on the day 910 days (130 weeks) before retirement age
-- is "within" the period.
GIVEN `the day of the injury` IS A DATE, `the day the worker reaches retirement age` IS A DATE
GIVETH AN `Age limit`
`ss 169, 171 -- the age limit on weekly payments` `the day of the injury` `the day the worker reaches retirement age` MEANS
    IF `days from` `the day of the injury` `to` `the day the worker reaches retirement age` AT MOST 910
    THEN `weekly payments for not more than the first 130 weeks of incapacity (s 169)`
    ELSE `weekly payments stop when the worker reaches retirement age (s 171)`

DECLARE `Reason for ending or reducing weekly payments` IS ONE OF
    `the expiry of the second entitlement period`
    `ceasing to be entitled to s 165 payments`
    `the employer withdrew the employment while s 165 payments were made`
    `another reason`

-- s 189(1), (3) (lines 2866-2881): if the worker has received weekly payments for a continuous period of at least
-- 12 weeks and has provided a certificate of capacity, the required period of notice is: 12 weeks to under one year,
-- 14 days; one year or more, 28 days; expiry of the second entitlement period, 13 weeks; ceasing s 165 payments,
-- 28 days; employer withdrawing the employment under s 165, 13 weeks. Outside s 189(1) the section sets none: NOTHING.
-- READING: "one year" is 52 weeks.
GIVEN `continuous weeks of weekly payments` IS A NUMBER
      `the worker has provided a certificate of capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reason` IS A `Reason for ending or reducing weekly payments`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 189 -- the days of notice before weekly payments are ended or reduced` `continuous weeks of weekly payments` `the worker has provided a certificate of capacity` `the reason` MEANS
    IF `continuous weeks of weekly payments` LESS THAN 12 OR (NOT `the worker has provided a certificate of capacity`)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER `the reason`
         WHEN `the expiry of the second entitlement period` THEN JUST 91
         WHEN `ceasing to be entitled to s 165 payments` THEN JUST 28
         WHEN `the employer withdrew the employment while s 165 payments were made` THEN JUST 91
         WHEN `another reason` THEN
            IF `continuous weeks of weekly payments` LESS THAN 52 THEN JUST 14 ELSE JUST 28

§§ `Part 5 Divisions 4 and 5 -- the impairment benefit (ss 197, 210, 211, 212, 217)`

-- s 197(2), (3) (lines 2964-2965): a Division 5 claim (other than for industrial deafness, an eligible progressive
-- disease, a further EPD injury, a serious lung injury or a lung transplant injury) "cannot be made before the expiry
-- of the period of 12 months after the date of the relevant injury"; but the Authority or self-insurer "may receive"
-- one earlier if the injury has stabilised.
GIVEN `the day of the injury` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 197(2) -- the first day an impairment benefit claim can be made` `the day of the injury` MEANS
    `days after` 1 (`months after` 12 `the day of the injury`)

GIVEN `the day of the injury` IS A DATE
      `the day of the claim` IS A DATE
      `the injury is industrial deafness, an eligible progressive disease, a further EPD injury, a serious lung injury or treated with lung transplant surgery` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the injury has stabilised` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 197(2), (3) -- an impairment benefit claim can be made on that day` `the day of the injury` `the day of the claim` `the injury is industrial deafness, an eligible progressive disease, a further EPD injury, a serious lung injury or treated with lung transplant surgery` `the injury has stabilised` IF
        `the injury is industrial deafness, an eligible progressive disease, a further EPD injury, a serious lung injury or treated with lung transplant surgery`
    OR  `the injury has stabilised`
    OR  DATE_SERIAL (`s 197(2) -- the first day an impairment benefit claim can be made` `the day of the injury`) AT MOST DATE_SERIAL `the day of the claim`

-- s 210(2) picks the impairment benefit rating; which description applies is an input.
DECLARE `How the rating is described` IS ONE OF
    `a modified whole person impairment (s 210(2)(a)(i))`
    `a modified spinal impairment (s 210(2)(a)(ii))`
    `a spinal impairment (s 210(2)(a)(iii), or a spinal impairment otherwise)`
    `any other whole person impairment`

-- s 210(1) (line 3129): relevant date: "(a) if the worker's impairment benefit rating is not more than 70 per cent,
-- the date of the relevant injury; or (b) if ... more than 70 per cent, the date on which the calculation is made".
GIVEN `the rating` IS A NUMBER, `the day of the injury` IS A DATE, `the day of the calculation` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 210(1) -- the relevant date` `the rating` `the day of the injury` `the day of the calculation` MEANS
    IF `the rating` AT MOST 70 THEN `the day of the injury` ELSE `the day of the calculation`

-- s 211(2) (lines 3145-3170), with the varied amounts for the year (the Act's figures in brackets):
-- (a) under 10: nil. (b)(i) a modified whole person impairment from 10 to under 11: $11 670 + (D - 10) x $9940;
-- (b)(ii) a modified spinal impairment from 10 to under 11: that x 1.1. (c)(i) 10 to 30, (b) not applying:
-- $18 810 + (D - 10) x $2830; (c)(ii) a spinal impairment from 10 to under 30, (b) not applying: the lesser of that x
-- 1.1 and $18 810 + 20 x $2830. (d) over 30 to 70: $75 260 + (D - 30) x $4700. (e) over 70 to 80: the lesser of
-- $262 070 + (D - 70) x $29 330 and $555 350. (f) over 80: $555 350.
GIVEN `the year` IS A `Figures year`
      `D` IS A NUMBER
      `the description` IS A `How the rating is described`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 211(2) -- the non-economic loss for permanent impairment` `the year` `D` `the description` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `D` LESS THAN 10 THEN 0
           IF `D` LESS THAN 11 AND `is modified whole person` `the description` THEN `b base` PLUS ((`D` MINUS 10) TIMES `b step`)
           IF `D` LESS THAN 11 AND `is modified spinal` `the description` THEN (`b base` PLUS ((`D` MINUS 10) TIMES `b step`)) TIMES 1.1
           IF `D` LESS THAN 30 AND `is spinal` `the description` THEN min ((`c base` PLUS ((`D` MINUS 10) TIMES `c step`)) TIMES 1.1) (`c base` PLUS (20 TIMES `c step`))
           IF `D` AT MOST 30 THEN `c base` PLUS ((`D` MINUS 10) TIMES `c step`)
           IF `D` AT MOST 70 THEN `d base` PLUS ((`D` MINUS 30) TIMES `d step`)
           IF `D` AT MOST 80 THEN min (`e base` PLUS ((`D` MINUS 70) TIMES `e step`)) `the maximum`
           OTHERWISE `the maximum`
    WHERE
        `b base` MEANS `the varied amount` `the s 211(2)(b) starting amount` `for` `the year`
        `b step` MEANS `the varied amount` `the s 211(2)(b) amount for each percentage point` `for` `the year`
        `c base` MEANS `the varied amount` `the s 211(2)(c) and s 212(b) starting amount` `for` `the year`
        `c step` MEANS `the varied amount` `the s 211(2)(c) and s 212(b) amount for each percentage point` `for` `the year`
        `d base` MEANS `the varied amount` `the s 211(2)(d) and s 212(c) starting amount` `for` `the year`
        `d step` MEANS `the varied amount` `the s 211(2)(d) and s 212(c) amount for each percentage point` `for` `the year`
        `e base` MEANS `the varied amount` `the s 211(2)(e) and s 212(d) starting amount` `for` `the year`
        `e step` MEANS `the varied amount` `the s 211(2)(e) and s 212(d) amount for each percentage point` `for` `the year`
        `the maximum` MEANS `the varied amount` `the maximum for non-economic loss` `for` `the year`

GIVEN `the description` IS A `How the rating is described`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is modified whole person` `the description` IF
    CONSIDER `the description`
    WHEN `a modified whole person impairment (s 210(2)(a)(i))` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the description` IS A `How the rating is described`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is modified spinal` `the description` IF
    CONSIDER `the description`
    WHEN `a modified spinal impairment (s 210(2)(a)(ii))` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 211(2)(c)(ii): "a spinal impairment (within the meaning of section 210(2)(a)(ii) or (iii))" -- a modified spinal
-- impairment of 11 or more is one too.
GIVEN `the description` IS A `How the rating is described`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is spinal` `the description` IF
    CONSIDER `the description`
    WHEN `a modified spinal impairment (s 210(2)(a)(ii))` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a spinal impairment (s 210(2)(a)(iii), or a spinal impairment otherwise)` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 212 (lines 3173-3185): psychiatric impairment. (a) under 30: nil. (b) 30: $18 810 + (D - 10) x $2830. (c) over 30
-- to 70: $75 260 + (D - 30) x $4700. (d) over 70 to 80: the lesser of $262 070 + (D - 70) x $29 330 and $555 530.
-- (e) over 80: $555 530. The Gazette prints the same varied maximum for s 212(d)(ii) and (e) as for s 211 (lines 567,
-- 570); NOTES.md finding 1.
GIVEN `the year` IS A `Figures year`, `D` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 212 -- the non-economic loss for permanent psychiatric impairment` `the year` `D` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `D` LESS THAN 30 THEN 0
           IF `D` EQUALS 30 THEN `c base` PLUS ((`D` MINUS 10) TIMES `c step`)
           IF `D` AT MOST 70 THEN `d base` PLUS ((`D` MINUS 30) TIMES `d step`)
           IF `D` AT MOST 80 THEN min (`e base` PLUS ((`D` MINUS 70) TIMES `e step`)) `the maximum`
           OTHERWISE `the maximum`
    WHERE
        `c base` MEANS `the varied amount` `the s 211(2)(c) and s 212(b) starting amount` `for` `the year`
        `c step` MEANS `the varied amount` `the s 211(2)(c) and s 212(b) amount for each percentage point` `for` `the year`
        `d base` MEANS `the varied amount` `the s 211(2)(d) and s 212(c) starting amount` `for` `the year`
        `d step` MEANS `the varied amount` `the s 211(2)(d) and s 212(c) amount for each percentage point` `for` `the year`
        `e base` MEANS `the varied amount` `the s 211(2)(e) and s 212(d) starting amount` `for` `the year`
        `e step` MEANS `the varied amount` `the s 211(2)(e) and s 212(d) amount for each percentage point` `for` `the year`
        `the maximum` MEANS `the varied amount` `the maximum for non-economic loss` `for` `the year`

-- s 217(1), (2) and s 219: no more than the maximum for several injuries on one occasion, or several kinds of
-- non-economic loss for one injury.
GIVEN `the year` IS A `Figures year`, `the total of the amounts` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 217 -- the non-economic loss after the limit` `the year` `the total of the amounts` MEANS
    min `the total of the amounts` (`the varied amount` `the maximum for non-economic loss` `for` `the year`)

§§ `Part 5 Division 8 -- compensation for the death of a worker (ss 234, 236, 237, 237A)`

DECLARE `Dependant's place` IS ONE OF
    `a dependent partner`
    `a dependent child`

-- s 236(1)-(5) (lines 3540-3561). The share of one dependant, worked from the numbers of dependent partners and
-- dependent children. NOTHING where the amount is a share the court, Authority or self-insurer "considers is
-- reasonable and appropriate" (s 236(6): no dependent partner and a dependent child who is not an orphan; s 237(1): a
-- partially dependent partner) or where s 236 does not reach (no dependent partner or child; the asker's place not
-- among the dependants).
GIVEN `the year` IS A `Figures year`
      `the asker is` IS A `Dependant's place`
      `the number of dependent partners` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of dependent children` IS A NUMBER
      `every dependent child is an orphan child` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the worker leaves a partially dependent partner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 236 -- the share of the lump sum` `the year` `the asker is` `the number of dependent partners` `the number of dependent children` `every dependent child is an orphan child` `the worker leaves a partially dependent partner` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the worker leaves a partially dependent partner` THEN NOTHING
           IF `P` AT LEAST 1 AND `C` EQUALS 0 THEN
              (CONSIDER `the asker is`
               WHEN `a dependent partner` THEN JUST (`the total` DIVIDED BY `P`)
               OTHERWISE NOTHING)
           IF `P` EQUALS 0 AND `C` AT LEAST 1 AND `every dependent child is an orphan child` THEN
              (CONSIDER `the asker is`
               WHEN `a dependent child` THEN JUST (`the total` DIVIDED BY `C`)
               OTHERWISE NOTHING)
           IF `P` AT LEAST 1 AND `C` EQUALS 1 THEN
              (CONSIDER `the asker is`
               WHEN `a dependent child` THEN JUST `the one child's amount`
               WHEN `a dependent partner` THEN JUST ((`the total` MINUS `the one child's amount`) DIVIDED BY `P`))
           IF `P` AT LEAST 1 AND `C` AT LEAST 2 AND `C` AT MOST 5 THEN
              (CONSIDER `the asker is`
               WHEN `a dependent child` THEN JUST `each child's amount`
               WHEN `a dependent partner` THEN JUST ((`the total` MINUS (`C` TIMES `each child's amount`)) DIVIDED BY `P`))
           IF `P` AT LEAST 1 AND `C` GREATER THAN 5 THEN
              (CONSIDER `the asker is`
               WHEN `a dependent partner` THEN JUST (`the partners' amount` DIVIDED BY `P`)
               WHEN `a dependent child` THEN JUST ((`the total` MINUS `the partners' amount`) DIVIDED BY `C`))
           OTHERWISE NOTHING
    WHERE
        `the total` MEANS `the varied amount` `the lump sum on the death of a worker` `for` `the year`
        `the one child's amount` MEANS `the varied amount` `the s 236(3)(a) amount for the one dependent child` `for` `the year`
        `each child's amount` MEANS `the varied amount` `the s 236(4)(a) amount for each dependent child` `for` `the year`
        `the partners' amount` MEANS `the varied amount` `the s 236(5)(a) amount for the dependent partners` `for` `the year`
        `P` MEANS `the number of dependent partners`
        `C` MEANS `the number of dependent children`

-- s 237A(2) (lines 3587-3591): "close family member of a worker means a person who, at the time of the worker's
-- death -- (a) was a partner, parent, guardian, step-parent, grandparent, sibling or step-sibling of the worker or a
-- person to whom the worker was a parent, step-parent or guardian; and (b) had a genuine personal relationship with
-- the worker." A "means" definition: outside it, no.
DECLARE `Relationship to the worker` IS ONE OF
    `partner`
    `parent`
    `guardian`
    `step-parent`
    `grandparent`
    `sibling`
    `step-sibling`
    `a person to whom the worker was a parent, step-parent or guardian`
    `none of these`

GIVEN `the relationship` IS A `Relationship to the worker`
      `a genuine personal relationship with the worker` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 237A(2) -- is a close family member` `the relationship` `a genuine personal relationship with the worker` IF
        `a genuine personal relationship with the worker`
    AND (CONSIDER `the relationship`
         WHEN `none of these` THEN FALSE
         OTHERWISE TRUE)

-- s 237A(1): "the amount of compensation payable on the death of the worker to each close family member of the
-- worker is $10 000" (varied).
GIVEN `the year` IS A `Figures year`
      `the relationship` IS A `Relationship to the worker`
      `a genuine personal relationship with the worker` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 237A(1) -- the grief and loss amount` `the year` `the relationship` `a genuine personal relationship with the worker` MEANS
    IF `s 237A(2) -- is a close family member` `the relationship` `a genuine personal relationship with the worker`
    THEN `the varied amount` `the s 237A(1) amount for each close family member` `for` `the year`
    ELSE 0

§§ `Part 7 Division 2 -- damages and the serious injury gateway (ss 325, 328, 330, 335, 340)`

DECLARE `Serious injury gateway` IS ONE OF
    `deemed a serious injury: impairment assessed at 30 per cent or more (s 335(1))`
    `deemed a serious injury: no written advice within the time (s 330(3))`
    `damages only with the certificate of the Authority or self-insurer, or the leave of a court (s 335(2))`

-- s 330(1) (line 5169): advise the worker in writing "within 120 days ... of receiving the application", with
-- s 329A disregarding 24 December to 9 January. (s 329, time hindering a medical examination, is out.)
GIVEN `the day the application was received` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 330(1) -- the last day to advise on a serious injury application` `the day the application was received` MEANS
    `days after, disregarding 24 December to 9 January,` 120 `the day the application was received`

-- s 335(1) (line 5213): an assessment of 30 per cent or more, made before the application, deems a serious injury.
-- s 330(3) (line 5178): no advice in time deems a serious injury. Otherwise s 335(2).
GIVEN `the assessment before the application, per cent` IS A NUMBER
      `the day the application was received` IS A DATE
      `written advice has been given` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day written advice was given` IS A DATE
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Serious injury gateway`
`ss 330, 335 -- the serious injury gateway` `the assessment before the application, per cent` `the day the application was received` `written advice has been given` `the day written advice was given` `the day asked about` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the assessment before the application, per cent` AT LEAST 30 THEN `deemed a serious injury: impairment assessed at 30 per cent or more (s 335(1))`
           IF `s 330(3) -- no advice was given in time` THEN `deemed a serious injury: no written advice within the time (s 330(3))`
           OTHERWISE `damages only with the certificate of the Authority or self-insurer, or the leave of a court (s 335(2))`
    WHERE
        `the last day` MEANS `s 330(1) -- the last day to advise on a serious injury application` `the day the application was received`
        `s 330(3) -- no advice was given in time` MEANS
                (NOT (`the day asked about` `is on or before` `the last day`))
            AND (   (NOT `written advice has been given`)
                 OR (NOT (`the day written advice was given` `is on or before` `the last day`)))

-- s 330(1), (3), as a rule. Clock: days from receiving the application; the number of days to the s 330(1) day is
-- worked out with s 329A and passed in.
GIVEN `the days to advise` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `WIRC party` `WIRC action`
`s 330 -- the Authority or self-insurer must advise on a serious injury application within 120 days` `the days to advise` MEANS
    PARTY `the Authority or self-insurer`
    MUST  `advise the worker in writing on the serious injury application`
    WITHIN `the days to advise`
    LEST  BREACH BY `the Authority or self-insurer` BECAUSE "s 330(1), (3): no written advice within 120 days of receiving the application, so the worker is deemed to have suffered a serious injury"

-- s 328(2)(b) (line 5135): an application on the ground of serious injury "only after a period of at least 18 months
-- has elapsed since the event or circumstance giving rise to the injury occurred". READING: the first day is the day
-- after the same date 18 months later.
GIVEN `the day of the event` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 328(2)(b) -- the first day a serious injury application can be made` `the day of the event` MEANS
    `days after` 1 (`months after` 18 `the day of the event`)

-- s 335(2)(d)(i) (line 5222): leave applied for "within 30 days after the worker received advice under section
-- 330(1)", disregarding 24 December to 9 January (s 329A); later only with the Authority's consent (s 337(1)).
GIVEN `the day the worker received the advice` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 335(2)(d)(i) -- the last day to apply to a court for leave` `the day the worker received the advice` MEANS
    `days after, disregarding 24 December to 9 January,` 30 `the day the worker received the advice`

GIVEN `the days to apply` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `WIRC party` `WIRC action`
`s 335(2)(d), s 337(1) -- apply for leave within 30 days, or only with the Authority's consent` `the days to apply` MEANS
    PARTY `the worker`
    DO    `apply to a court for leave to bring proceedings for damages`
    WITHIN `the days to apply`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST
        PARTY `the worker`
        MAY   `ask the Authority to consent to a late application for leave`

-- s 325(2)(e)-(g) (lines 5092-5104): relying on loss of earning capacity, the worker must have "a loss of earning
-- capacity of 40 per cent or more" (measured by (f): the greater of what the worker earns and could earn in suitable
-- employment, against the pre-injury earning capacity over 3 years before and after the injury), continue
-- permanently to have a loss "productive of financial loss of 40 per cent or more", and not have (g) a capacity for
-- any employment that would earn "more than 60 per cent". (e)(i): for a worker under 26 at the injury or in Schedule 2
-- item 1, the loss is not measured by (f), and the Act says no other way: NOTHING. These are requirements only: the
-- court or the Authority still has to be satisfied the injury is "serious" (s 325(2)(b), (c)).
GIVEN `the worker was under 26 at the injury or is in Schedule 2 item 1` IS A BOOLEAN
      `yearly income now (the greater of earned and able to be earned in suitable employment)` IS A NUMBER
      `yearly income before the injury (s 325(2)(f)(ii))` IS A NUMBER
      `yearly income the worker could earn with a capacity for any employment, after rehabilitation or retraining` IS A NUMBER
      `the loss will continue permanently to be productive of financial loss of 40 per cent or more` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 325(2)(e)-(g) -- the loss of earning capacity requirements are met` `the worker was under 26 at the injury or is in Schedule 2 item 1` `yearly income now (the greater of earned and able to be earned in suitable employment)` `yearly income before the injury (s 325(2)(f)(ii))` `yearly income the worker could earn with a capacity for any employment, after rehabilitation or retraining` `the loss will continue permanently to be productive of financial loss of 40 per cent or more` MEANS
    IF `the worker was under 26 at the injury or is in Schedule 2 item 1` OR `yearly income before the injury (s 325(2)(f)(ii))` AT MOST 0
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (    (`yearly income before the injury (s 325(2)(f)(ii))` MINUS `yearly income now (the greater of earned and able to be earned in suitable employment)`) AT LEAST (0.4 TIMES `yearly income before the injury (s 325(2)(f)(ii))`)
               AND `the loss will continue permanently to be productive of financial loss of 40 per cent or more`
               AND (NOT (`yearly income the worker could earn with a capacity for any employment, after rehabilitation or retraining` GREATER THAN (0.6 TIMES `yearly income before the injury (s 325(2)(f)(ii))`))))

-- s 340 (lines 5253-5261): no pecuniary loss damages if the total assessed before reductions is less than the
-- threshold, none in excess of the maximum; the same for pain and suffering. The varied amounts are "as at the date of
-- the award". READING: the threshold is tested on the total before reductions, as the text says; the maximum is
-- applied to the same total (whether before or after the s 343 and contributory negligence reductions is not said;
-- NOTES.md finding 4).
GIVEN `the threshold` IS A NUMBER, `the maximum` IS A NUMBER, `the total assessed before reductions` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 340 -- the damages that may be awarded` `the threshold` `the maximum` `the total assessed before reductions` MEANS
    IF `the total assessed before reductions` LESS THAN `the threshold`
    THEN 0
    ELSE min `the total assessed before reductions` `the maximum`
